WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.215 --> 00:00:02.882
(curious music)

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.063
- First off, Magformers are fun.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.633
It's magnetic construction.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.080
I'm the CEO fro Magformers.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.253
We're a toy company.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.940
On December 27th, we
had a lot of work to do

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:29.000
in closing out our year.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.283
A lot of happiness early in the morning.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:35.170
Some of our toys received awards

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:39.343
and excitement of seeing
2018 come to an end.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.670
It was mid-morning when all of a sudden

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:45.260
we had two of our employees

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:48.250
race from different
directions in the office.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.680
They both were bringing
the same communication,

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.180
and that is that a child
had swallowed Magformers.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:59.420
- Jennifer White thought
this small piece of plastic

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.400
was a unique Christmas gift.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.670
Instead, the magnets inside of it

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:06.050
left hols throughout her son's stomach.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:08.140
- They were doing what magnets do,

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.430
and try to get to each other
through his intestines,

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:14.973
and it created holes in the lining.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.370
- [Narrator] The toy
that caused the injury

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:19.843
was purchased on Amazon.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.530
The Wall Street Journal
set out to investigate

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:25.580
how many unsafe products like this

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.923
are on Amazon's massive Marketplace.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.420
The toy gifted to the White family

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:33.480
wasn't actually Magformers;

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.750
rather, it was one of the
many similar-looking products

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:37.973
for sale on Amazon by a third party.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:44.150
- 300,000 social media hits later,

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:48.240
the father of the child
identified the product,

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.263
called IMDEN.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:53.780
It was taken off Amazon's site.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:54.683
It should've been.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.633
Unsafe.

00:01:57.633 --> 00:02:00.300
(curious music)

00:02:14.257 --> 00:02:17.240
- [Narrator] When Amazon CEO
Jeff Bezos started the company,

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.833
he decided to sell books
for a simple reason.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.430
There are a lot of books.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.010
- Books were great, because books

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.630
are incredibly unusual in one respect,

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:30.850
and that is that there are
more items in the book category

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.373
than there are items in
any other category by far.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:35.950
- [Narrator] As Amazon has grown,

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:39.210
Bezos and other top Amazon
executives have emphasized

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:43.420
selection as a key aspect of
Amazon's business philosophy.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.870
- If you can focus obsessively enough

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.340
on customer experience: selection.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:51.480
We keep pursuing that notion
of Earth's biggest selection.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.930
It's selection.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:56.530
The three big ideas are low prices,

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:00.943
fast delivery, and vast selection.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:04.340
- [Narrator] Search
"magnetic toy" on Amazon

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.750
and you're presented with
an avalanche of choices:

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:09.933
colors, shapes, number of pieces, price.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.810
In 2001, Jeff Bezos came up

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:16.580
with his theory of the virtuous cycle.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:18.210
According to Amazon executives,

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:20.580
Bezos originally sketched it on a napkin,

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:23.943
and it has since become an
important part of Amazon's story.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.790
- So our virtuous cycle starts

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:28.590
with a terrific customer experience.

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:32.490
- [Narrator] It uses the
concept of a flywheel,

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.880
a heavy wheel that's
hard to turn initially

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.440
but generates its own momentum

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.853
and becomes self-reinforcing
once it gets going.

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:43.160
In Amazon's case it goes like this:

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.980
greater selection and lower prices

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:47.600
lead to greater customer satisfaction,

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:50.050
which leads to more site visits,

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:52.970
which makes it more attractive
for third-party sellers,

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:56.070
which increases selection
and simultaneously leads

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:59.880
to lower overhead for
Amazon, which lowers prices,

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.623
and round and round it goes.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.980
This theory was one of the
reasons why Amazon built

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:09.370
its Marketplace, which
has grown to include

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:11.273
millions of third-party sellers.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.350
In the view of its
executives, more sellers

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.973
means more selection driving
their virtuous cycle.

00:04:19.330 --> 00:04:21.500
- They bring selection that is really hard

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.100
for us to get ourselves,

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:25.150
and that adds to the customer experience.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:29.820
- What's probably the most
surprising to most consumers

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:32.550
is the fact that most
products sold on Amazon

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.193
are not sold by Amazon itself.

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:39.530
What best describes Amazon
is it's a company of systems.

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.420
Most of the large businesses we build

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:44.710
not only have flywheels,
but they also have systems,

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:46.510
which means they can be scaled,

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:47.963
usually without any limit.

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.780
- [Narrator] An Amazon spokeswoman
said the company's goals

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:55.800
of unbeatable price,
selection, and convenience

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:58.050
don't come at the expense
of customer safety.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.510
Since Jeff Bezos made his napkin drawing,

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.240
third-party sales have
grown from 6% of sales

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.953
on Amazon to nearly 60%.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.460
And as this Marketplace
has exploded in size,

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:17.143
so too has the need to balance
selection and product safety.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.860
The Wall Street Journal conducted
a search of Amazon's site

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:23.840
for items declared unsafe
by government agencies

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.620
or that are deceptively labeled,

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.740
products that big-box
retailers won't sell.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:32.730
The journal's investigation
found about 4,100 such products

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:37.160
for sale on Amazon, and an
additional 6,700 balloons

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:39.683
that lacked federally-mandated
warning labels.

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:44.670
83% of the listings
were updates or removed

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:47.603
after the journal sent Amazon
the products it identified.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.900
The Food and Drug Administration warns

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:54.180
this sort of sleeping mat
can suffocate infants.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.330
Amazon bans them from their Marketplace,

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:59.163
but the journal found 80
for sale on the site anyway.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:03.900
Amazon removed all of the
infant sleep positioners

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.193
the journal identified.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.210
- The challenge for Amazon is that

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:10.860
what built the Amazon Marketplace,

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:13.560
it being so open and so
welcoming to new sellers,

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.430
it has also meant that, today,

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.090
Amazon is really having a hard time

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:19.160
enforcing many of its own rules,

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:21.070
because it just physically cannot allocate

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:23.853
enough human power to
police many of these rules.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:27.010
- [Narrator] Within two
weeks of Amazon's removing

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:29.100
or altering problematic listings,

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:32.970
130 items with the same
policy violations reappeared,

00:06:32.970 --> 00:06:35.023
some sold by the same vendors.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:39.390
An Amazon spokeswoman said
it removed these items

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:41.433
and refined its tools for catching them.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.160
She added that the company's tools

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:46.940
prevent most non-compliant listings

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:48.540
from ever appearing on the site.

00:06:49.630 --> 00:06:52.070
And when sellers manage
to evade its systems,

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:53.890
Amazon acts quickly to remove items

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.390
and penalize the offending seller.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.000
Additionally, she said the company

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.730
provides resources to
sellers about proper labeling

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:03.234
and other compliance obligations.

00:07:03.234 --> 00:07:06.151
(intriguing music)

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:16.360
- The Marketplace was very clearly set up

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:18.740
to be an independent entity

00:07:18.740 --> 00:07:22.400
where people could use the
technology that Amazon had built

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:24.713
but not necessarily be part of Amazon.

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:28.340
My name is Rachel Johnson Grier,

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:31.130
and I've been working in
this consultant business

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.320
that I started four years ago.

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.690
We help sellers on Amazon Marketplace.

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:38.100
I worked at Amazon for about eight years,

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.960
and my first role in
compliance was handling

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:43.283
all of recalls and product
safety for North America.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:46.750
I got very familiar with how
Amazon enforced on sellers,

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:49.320
how they communicated with sellers.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.070
We can say that we're
not going to interfere

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:54.170
in the Marketplace, but as
soon as customers are upset

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:57.113
or someone could get hurt,
now we have a problem.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.750
- [Narrator] In 2011, the Consumer Product

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.430
Safety Commission, or CPSC, issued recalls

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:06.450
for many drop-side cribs as
the news media and public

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:08.800
grew increasingly concerned
about their safety.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.440
- [Reporter] The largest
baby crib recall in history

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:15.263
involves more than two
million drop-side cribs.

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:21.700
- The CPSC was trying to
redesign their crib regulations,

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:23.770
and all cribs had to
meet the new regulation,

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:25.270
I believe it was by June 2011.

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:29.300
Working with recalls,
normally what we would do

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:32.270
is we would remove everything from Amazon.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:34.637
I was like, "Then let's
remove all the cribs,

00:08:34.637 --> 00:08:35.797
"and then anything that comes back

00:08:35.797 --> 00:08:37.270
"is guaranteed to be compliant."

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:39.430
I was told that they didn't
want to take things down,

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:41.310
because it would limit selection.

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:43.500
That's what they're incentivized to do:

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.963
more selection, more sales.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.630
As a compliance person,
you're incentivized

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:52.210
to either meet the law
or protect customers,

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:54.453
and those two did not go together.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:57.720
At the time, I was about
six months pregnant,

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:01.050
and what I argued to
them was that no mother,

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:02.950
no mother ever wants selection

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:05.660
that's going to hurt her child, ever.

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:08.070
And I lost the argument.

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:11.060
And that has ...

00:09:11.060 --> 00:09:12.710
That has been painful ever since.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:16.630
- [Narrator] An Amazon
spokeswoman said the company

00:09:16.630 --> 00:09:20.160
executes recalls as soon
as it is aware of them,

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.980
and requires sellers to
meet any new requirements

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:24.773
the CPSC introduces.

00:09:26.314 --> 00:09:30.430
(intriguing string music)

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:33.970
What does it take to ensure
a safe children's product?

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:35.810
The Wall Street Journal
ordered a selection

00:09:35.810 --> 00:09:38.370
of children's toys that
are popular on Amazon

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:41.193
and sent them to a
federally-certified lab for testing.

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:43.950
They were subjected to drop tests,

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:46.363
torque tests, chemical tests, and more.

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:51.533
Of the 10 toys the journal
sent for testing, four failed.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:54.310
One of those was this xylophone

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:56.850
from the AILUKI toddler
musical instruments set,

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:58.630
which was found to contain four times

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:01.290
the federal limit of lead for children.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:04.320
The company disputed the
results and sent a test report

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:07.083
from a different laboratory
showing a passing result.

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:10.740
The journal spoke to safety
and compliance experts

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.810
who said this discrepancy should trigger

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:15.690
a halt to sales and more testing.

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:19.830
And Amazon removed these
items from their marketplace.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:22.610
Government officials are
also turning their attentions

00:10:22.610 --> 00:10:25.563
to the dangers posed by some
products sold on Amazon.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:28.510
- So we're here to announce
today that Amazon will commit

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:31.660
to legally-binding,
nationwide corporate reforms

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:35.830
after my office found dozens
of children's school supplies

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:38.480
and jewelry sold on its Marketplace

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:41.853
had illegal levels of toxic metals.

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:45.170
We just had some suspicions
that there were products

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:48.380
out there for sale that
had not adequately tested

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:49.890
and were not compliant with the law

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.190
and not safe for children.

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:55.710
We tested about a hundred Amazon products.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:58.563
More than half had illegal
amounts of lead and cadmium.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:02.370
That's not a great track
record to start with.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:05.170
Kids with their toys, with
their school supplies,

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:07.240
if they're anything like my
kids when they were young,

00:11:07.240 --> 00:11:09.530
they're chewing on those things,
they're sleeping with them,

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:12.950
they are in close proximity,
often for many hours a day.

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:14.560
Across the country, consumers made

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:17.483
more than 15,000 purchases
of these products.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:19.740
So it led to a settlement.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:22.130
Amazon in this case has to see the state,

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:24.537
make consumers hold for what they pay for,

00:11:24.537 --> 00:11:27.640
and most importantly change
the corporate practices

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:29.620
and detail what that looks like.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:31.600
- [Narrator] An Amazon
spokeswoman said the company

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:34.550
welcomes ongoing collaboration
with the Attorney General

00:11:34.550 --> 00:11:36.203
to promote customer safety.

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:39.443
- The only real way to know, as Amazon,

00:11:39.443 --> 00:11:41.610
that the products that are
being sold on the website

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:43.780
are compliant is to pull it
from the fulfillment center,

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:46.293
send it to a lab themselves,
and get it tested.

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:50.240
Because otherwise, paperwork is paperwork.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:51.883
You could just make up whatever you want.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:55.040
- [Narrator] Not only are
there a lot of unsafe products

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.900
on Amazon; many of them
sold by third parties

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.803
imitate safe, popular items.

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:05.440
- Amazon Marketplace means
anyone can sell anything,

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:07.040
which also means, if you're a bad actor

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:10.470
trying to sell an unsafe
product, a counterfeit product,

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:12.633
a wrongly-named product ...

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:14.883
you can.

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:17.290
- [Narrator] A lot of the work rooting out

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:19.630
bad sellers on Amazon's Marketplace

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:22.453
is done not by Amazon
but by other sellers.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.860
- Our binder against counterfeit

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:30.040
has been going on since 2012.

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:32.960
I mean, how many times
have some of these changed

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:35.340
from one name to another on Amazon?

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:38.840
- Oh, they tend to change very quickly,

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:41.030
or they're sold under various names.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:43.070
- [Chris Tidwell] Which one is ours?

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:44.740
- These two are ours.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:46.690
These two are counterfeit.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:50.920
There's almost no real
distinction between the packaging.

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:53.120
So when mom and dad get it home,

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:56.060
they won't know that something's amiss.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:57.610
And that's our biggest concern.

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:00.853
We are showing you how ...

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:04.492
easy it is to break one of the knockoffs.

00:13:04.492 --> 00:13:06.742
(snapping)

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:09.630
And these magnets are not
something you want laying

00:13:09.630 --> 00:13:12.323
around your house if you
have small children or pets.

00:13:15.359 --> 00:13:17.220
- [Narrator] An Amazon
spokeswoman said the company

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:20.563
investigates claims and takes
action against bad actors.

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:24.080
She said Amazon also gives sellers tools

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:26.653
to remove unsafe selection
and counterfeit items.

00:13:29.780 --> 00:13:33.060
She added that, in the case
of IMDEN magnetic toy blocks,

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.950
Amazon removed the item as soon

00:13:34.950 --> 00:13:37.063
as it became aware of the safety incident.

00:13:39.190 --> 00:13:42.140
The manufacturer of IMDEN
magnetic building blocks

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:43.273
declined to comment.

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.480
Amazon has gotten so big
and does so many things

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:51.540
that many ask, what is Amazon?

00:13:51.540 --> 00:13:53.793
Bezos himself has been
asked this question.

00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:55.960
- What is Amazon?

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:58.780
I would say really it's a
collection of principles,

00:13:58.780 --> 00:14:00.853
and it's an approach that we deploy.

00:14:02.790 --> 00:14:05.500
- [Narrator] But if these
principles conflict with safety,

00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:06.763
will they have to change?

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:09.760
- The things that they
claim to be possible

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:11.560
are just ultimately unprofitable.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:13.910
You could argue that many of these issues

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:15.957
can and will be solved by Amazon,

00:14:15.957 --> 00:14:18.670
but they will probably
require fundamentally changing

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:19.670
the building blocks.

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:24.460
- I believe Amazon has the
ability to do anything they want.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:27.930
They're the strongest and
most powerful retailer

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:31.613
at this point in the world.

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:37.290
- I in fact don't buy from
third-party sellers for my son,

00:14:37.290 --> 00:14:38.820
because I know that there's a risk there.

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:40.900
I typically will buy
from well-known brands,

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:42.060
and I will bay the extra,

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:44.060
because I know what I'm paying for.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:45.210
A lot of consumers don't,

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:47.860
or they don't have the
resources to make that choice.

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.610
- I'm under no illusion that somehow

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:52.720
our agreement with Amazon
is solving the problem

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:54.460
by any stretch of the imagination.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:57.740
But do want to communicate to
Amazon, "Hey, we're watching"?

00:14:57.740 --> 00:14:59.320
Yes.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:01.520
You don't get a pass
because you're really big

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:02.920
and it's really complicated.

00:15:04.138 --> 00:15:07.471
(soft electronic music)

